@trendifest/opendesk
===

This package contains source-derived UI code from the OpenDesk web application.

  Upstream:  https://github.com/useopendesk/opendesk
  Commit:    9f7e79072bb41c8be2bd0a96eaa74aba1333ce3c
  License:   Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE in this directory)
  Copyright: Copyright 2026 Mindroot Ltd

Upstream files adapted (paths relative to the upstream repository):

  web/src/styles/app.css            semantic light/dark tokens, base styles, utilities
  web/src/app/AppLayout.tsx         shell frame, inset work panel, collapsed nav rail
  web/src/app/Sidebar.tsx           full-height sidebar, scroll area, stable footer
  web/src/app/sidebarParts.tsx      navigation row shapes, labels, counts, section headers
  web/src/components/ui/button.tsx  Button
  web/src/components/ui/badge.tsx   Badge
  web/src/components/ui/dialog.tsx  Dialog
  web/src/components/ui/spinner.tsx Spinner
  web/src/lib/cn.ts                 class-name helper
  LICENSE                           copied verbatim

Bundled fonts (not part of the Apache-2.0 upstream): the latin subsets of Geist
and Geist Mono, copied from the Fontsource builds of the Vercel Geist fonts.
Both are licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, retained at
src/fonts/geist-OFL.txt and src/fonts/geist-mono-OFL.txt.

  Copyright 2024 The Geist Project Authors (https://github.com/vercel/geist-font)

Adaptations: the helpdesk application runtime (routing, session, i18n, realtime,
assistant, billing, telemetry), its domain components and its scripts were not
copied. Remaining components take their state from props. Variants, sizes and
palette tones with no consumer in this app were dropped: Button keeps primary,
secondary and ghost at two sizes, Badge keeps the neutral and ok tones, Dialog
keeps two widths. The dialog open/close motion and the foldable sidebar section
stay, limited to short CSS transitions/animations that are disabled by
prefers-reduced-motion, and Radix (scoped to @radix-ui/react-dialog) supplies
dialog focus trapping, Escape handling and ARIA semantics. Only the latin font
subsets are loaded; other scripts fall back to the platform UI font. Class names
are joined with clsx alone, and the few overrides that need to win over a
component default are settled by a component-layer rule, so no class-merging
runtime is bundled.

